108:When enabled, language model providers that support strict tool calling will only generate tool calls that are valid according to your defined `inputSchema`.
109:This increases the reliability of tool calling.
110:However, not all schemas may be supported in strict mode, and what is supported depends on the specific provider.
112:By default, strict mode is disabled. You can enable it per-tool by setting `strict: true`:
115:tool({
