161:By default, tools with an `execute` function run automatically as the model calls them. Configure approval with `toolApproval` on `generateText`, `streamText`, or `ToolLoopAgent`.
163:`toolApproval` can be either:
165:- A `GenericToolApprovalFunction` for all tool calls
166:- A per-tool map of statuses and/or `SingleToolApprovalFunction` callbacks (either function may return `undefined` for the same effect as `'not-applicable'`)
168:The older `needsApproval` property on `tool()` definitions is deprecated. Existing code still works, but new code should move approval logic to `toolApproval`.
170:### Configure `toolApproval`
175:  tools: { runCommand },
176:  toolApproval: {
183:In the per-tool object form, each key can be one of four statuses, either as a
186:- `'not-applicable'`: the tool is executed without an approval flow. This is the default behavior.
187:- `'approved'`: record an automatic approval by emitting approval request/response parts in the output, then execute the tool
188:- `'denied'`: record an automatic denial by emitting approval request/response parts in the output, then surface a denied tool output
195:toolApproval: {
